    83                                      ; Graphical forest menu. Drawing to the VBE LFB does NOT work from real /
    84                                      ; unreal mode on QEMU, so the menu is drawn from short 16-bit PROTECTED-MODE
    85                                      ; excursions (see run_in_pm) while keyboard/timer polling stays in real mode
    86                                      ; via INT 16h/INT 1Ah. If no suitable VBE mode is found, vesa_menu falls back
    87                                      ; to the plain text menu. The graphical mode is torn down (text 03h restored,
    88                                      ; framebuffer info cleared) before the kernel handoff, so the multiboot
    89                                      ; handoff is byte-identical to the proven text-mode path.
    90 00000182 C606[2F15]00                mov  byte [vesa_ok], 0
    91                                  
    92                                      ; Boot menu (graphical VBE, text fallback)
